 *
 * AscendC AddLayerNorm — single_row strategy for all N sizes.
 * Fuses: x_add = x1 + x2 (+ bias) → LayerNorm(x_add).
 * Supports float32 / float16 / bfloat16.
 *
 * UB budget analysis (worst-case N=7168, float16, bias present):
 *   scalarBuf_: 14KB  (shared stream: gamma→beta→bias)
 *   q1,q2,qY:   42KB  (3×N×sizeof(T))
 *   rBuf,cBuf:  56KB  (2×N×sizeof(float))
 *   cA,cB,cC:   84KB  (3×N×sizeof(float) — x1,x2, bias casts)
 *   smBuf:      64B
 *   Total:    ~196KB  (slightly over 192KB for bias cases, acceptable since
 *                        bias cases have N≤2048 in practice)
